    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="0852" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.1115/2191: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-07T12:00:00+00:00">November 7,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 7—11:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Line damaged and unable as yet to telephone Department’s 33 and 34 to
                        Vigo.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d787-f1"/> Stewart brought following message
                    from Graves: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Just received word from Auditor General at Coruna that Celaya<anchor
                                n="84" xml:id="d787-f2"/> will be tried by court martial at Lugo
                            Wednesday, November 11. Understand either death sentence or life
                            imprisonment will be requested. Am planning to be present at court
                            martial.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Department’s 33 and 34 delivered personally to Stewart.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d787-f1" n="83" xml:id="d787-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d787-f2" n="84" xml:id="d787-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram of October 17, 1 p.m., from the Consul General at Lisbon, <ref
                        target="#pg739">p. 739</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
